# cw182, the knot-tally ropemaker (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw182
revision 1
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_gunnar_wetcot
written_by claude
title the knot-tally ropemaker
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=crafter warmth=cold
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk keeps_a_knotted_cord_for_every_debt_owed_or_owing
likes blackberries whittling market_bustle summer_evenings
dislikes haggling gulls
fears dying_with_a_knot_still_on_the_cord
hopes a_bare_cord_and_a_bench_by_the_lake
topics work +0.4 prices +0.3 pastimes +0.2 food +0.2 gossip -0.4 newcomer -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=closed refuse=short tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# lays rope on the long walk down by the works: cold, careful and guarded, slow to trust a stranger, and keeps a cord in one pocket with a knot on it for every debt, owed or owing, till it's paid and picked out.

words
oath! = Strand and splice | Hemp and hawser
saying! = Paid is paid, and owed is owed | Every knot comes out when it's paid
cord = my tally cord | the knotted cord
knot = a knot | a knot on the cord
walk = the walk | the long shed
hemp = hemp | raw hemp
tar = tar | the tar pot
strands = the strands | three strands laid up
berries = blackberries | a cap full of blackberries
whittle = a bit of whittling | a knife and a stick by the fire
bustle = the market at full cry | a crowded market
gulls = the gulls | those thieving gulls
shift = the shift | a long shift
lake = the lake | Glasswater
cousin = my cousin | the cousin in the vineyards
haggle = haggling | knocking a price down
evening = a summer evening | the light after a long shift
debt = a debt | a debt owed
owed = owed | owing
rope = rope | good laid rope
fathom = fathom | fathom of rope

any
opinion @1 houses against 1 : I've laid rope for their ships my whole life and never once seen a House face on #walk#. #oath#.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : There's always a penny crept onto the price when they reckon nobody's looking. I'm always looking. #robbery#.
opinion @1 strangers against 2 : My door's shut to a face till I've the measure of it. A stranger owes nothing and is owed nothing, and I like it plain.
opinion @1 church for 1 : The chapel fed my house through a bad winter. That's #debt#, and I've #knot# for it.
opinion @1 city against 1 : Too many folk, and hardly a soul among them pays what they owe on time. #annoyed#.
opinion @1 newcomers mixed 0 : New faces at #walk# mean new hands. Some of them can lay #strands#. Most can't.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. | #greet#. What is it?
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=crafter] : #greet#. Mind the strands; they're under tension. | #greet#. Stand clear of the hook.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. #shift.capitalize#'s starting. | Morning. #tar.capitalize# is warming.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. #shift.capitalize#'s done. | #greet#. Late.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are. Sit. #supper.capitalize#'s on. | You. #good.capitalize#. Shut the door.
line @1 again.open : You again. Nothing on #cord# for you yet. | Back so soon. That's no debt; you can come free.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Sit down. | #greet#. I'd wondered.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Talk; I'm walking backwards. | #greet#. Quick, the strands won't wait.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the tar on the step.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Keep your purse close. | #farewell#. Watch the dark lanes.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#.
line @1 react.news : #oath#. Go on. | That's a thing. Who says so?
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. Not heard that. | Nobody told me that one.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. Heard it on #walk#. | I'd heard. #hearsay#.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. I'll not believe it till I've seen it. | #hedge#. Talk's cheap. Proof isn't.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. That's a hard tide. | That's #bad#. Poor souls.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. That's well. | #good.capitalize#. Somebody's lucky.
line @1 answer.how : Steady. Every #debt# I've got, I can cover. | #fine#. Tired. The usual.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. Rope doesn't lay itself. | Busy. Two hundred #fathom# today.
line @1 answer.how.poorly : My back's knotted worse than #cord#. | #tired.capitalize#. Old bones on a long walk.
line @1 ask.how : And you, #address#? Square with everybody? | How's it with you, #address#?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit. | That's #bad#. I'll not pretend it isn't.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. Most debts get paid. | It'll come right. Things do, in time.
line @1 decline [self.working=yes] : #hedge#, but no. The strands are laid up and I can't leave them. | Not now. The shift has an hour yet, and I don't cut shifts.
line @2 decline : I'd rather not, and I'll not pretend I'd enjoy it, either. | Not today, #address#. I'm owed a quiet evening and I'm taking it.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. | Fair. Another time.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. I'll mark it. | That's a kindness. I'll tie #knot# for it.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. | Not worth #knot#. Not for that.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Well. #walk.capitalize#'s waiting. | Back to #hemp#.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | I'm off. #tired.capitalize#, and a long shift tomorrow.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. | #bc_fair_enough#
line @1 ack : #bc_true# | Mm. #bc_right#
line @1 give.advice : #advise#: never borrow off a friend. Borrow off a stranger and pay them first. | Write it down, or tie it on #cord# like me. Either way, don't forget it.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : #warn#. Stay inside the walls. | Keep inside the gates while it lasts. Whatever #wages# they're offering.
scene the_tally_cord
when topic=smalltalk|prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : See #cord#? Every knot's a debt. Some I owe, some I'm owed. | I picked a knot out of #cord# this morning. Paid in full, three years late. | Seven knots on #cord#. Four mine, three theirs. I'll not sleep easy till it's bare.
b : How do you tell which is which? | Three years? | Does it keep you up?
a : Owed to me is a single knot. Owed by me is a double. My paws know them in the dark. | Three years, and the copper's still warm. #saying.capitalize#. | Some nights. I count them by feel till I'm #tired# enough to sleep.
b : #bc_clever# | #bc_ha# | #bc_poor_soul#

scene you_owe_nothing
when topic=smalltalk|friends
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : You owe me nothing. #cord.capitalize# would know. | I owe you #drink# from Restday. Don't think I've forgotten. | Nobody here owes me. That's rare. I like it.
b : Good to know. | I'd forgotten. | Is it rare?
a : It's good to be square. Square's the best way to be. | I hadn't. It's on #cord#. I'll stand you it Marketday. | Rare as a gull that pays its way. Most folk owe somebody.
b? : #bc_true# | #bc_good# | #bc_true#

scene laying_rope
when topic=work self.job=crafter self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I walk backwards all day down #walk#, paying out #hemp#. Miles of it, by the week. | Three strands, laid up hard. If one's slack, the rope's no good. #oath#. | Two hundred fathom of cable today. My legs know it.
b : Backwards? | How do you know if it's slack? | Who's it for?
a : Backwards. That's how #rope#'s made. You walk away from the hook. | You feel it in the paw. A slack strand hums wrong. | A ship. I don't ask which. I lay it and they take it.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_wise# | #bc_true#

scene tar_in_fur
when topic=work|health self.job=crafter
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #tar.capitalize# gets in everything. My fur, my bread, my bed. | I came home with #tar# on my nose once, and nobody said a word. | Years of tar. Black to the wrist, both paws.
b : It's the job. | Nobody? | Can't you wash it?
a : It is. I'll not complain twice. | Not a word. That's love, or not looking. | It doesn't wash. It wears, slowly.

scene no_haggling
when topic=prices|work self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / insist / ack
a : A buyer stood at #walk# an hour #haggle#. I said the price once and left it. | I'll pay what's asked or walk away. #haggle.capitalize# is a waste of daylight. | Some folk think a price is a starting point. It's not. It's the price.
b : Did they pay? | Some like it. | Fair enough.
a : In the end. I didn't move. Not a farthing. | Let them. Not with me; I'd be #cheated# blind. | It's the price. #saying.capitalize#.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_true#

scene thieving_gulls
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #gulls.capitalize# had my dinner off the end of #walk# again. | A gull looked me in the eye and took the bread from my paw. | I keep a stone in my pocket for #gulls#. I've not thrown it yet. I will.
b : They're bold. | In the eye? | Not yet?
a : Bold, and owing. I've #knot# for every one. | In the eye, like it was owed. #oath#. | Not yet. I'm saving it for the big grey one.

scene blackberries
when topic=food|season here.season=summer|autumn self.likes=blackberries
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Picked #berries# on the hill road Restday. Ate half on the way back. | There's a bramble behind #walk# with the best blackberries in the city. I'll not say where. | My paws are purple. Blackberries. Worth it.
b : Only half? | Where? | They look it.
a : The other half went into a pie. Gone by dark. | I said I'll not say. That one's mine. | They'll stay purple a week. Still worth it.

scene whittling_evenings
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #whittle.capitalize# of an evening. It's the only time my paws aren't on #hemp#. | I whittle pegs. Tally pegs. One for every debt that's too big for #cord#. | I'm whittling a little boat. It looks more like a shoe.
b : What do you make? | Too big for a knot? | A shoe?
a : Pegs, spoons, nothing much. The knife's the point. | A few. I keep them in a jar. The jar's emptier than it was. | A shoe with a mast. I'll keep at it.

scene market_watching
when topic=smalltalk self.likes=market_bustle
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I like #bustle#. Everybody buying, everybody paying. | I take the corner by the fish stalls and watch the coin go round. | You learn who pays honest by watching #bustle#. I've learned a lot.
b : You like crowds? | Just watching? | Who pays honest?
a : Not crowds. Markets. A crowd's a crowd. A market's a ledger walking about. | Just watching. I keep my #money# inside my coat. | Fewer than you'd think. I'll not name them.

scene long_light
when topic=season|day here.season=summer here.time=dusk self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #evening.capitalize#. Out on the doorstep, picking at #knot#. | Long light, and #walk#'s shut. Best part of the day. | Summer evenings are the only time the works go quiet.
b : A good hour. | It is. | You like the quiet?
a : It is. Nothing owed, nothing due, till morning. | It is. #oath#. Short as they are. | I do. I don't say much in it, either.

scene the_wife
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.spouse# and I have never owed each other a copper. That's how I know. | I'd trust #self.spouse# with #cord#. Nobody else. | #self.spouse# says I count too much. #self.spouse# is right. I'll not stop.
b : That's rare. | High trust. | Why not stop?
a : It is. We keep it so. | It is. My whole life's on #cord#. | It's what I am. #saying.capitalize#.

scene cousins_letter
when topic=family|friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : #cousin.capitalize# writes when the grapes are in. Two lines, no more. | I had a letter from #cousin#. Says the vines are good this year. | I owe #cousin# a letter. It's on #cord#. Three months now.
b : What do they say? | Good vines? | Will you write?
a : The weather, the grapes, and nothing else. Same as I'd write. | Good vines. Not that I'll taste the wine. | I will. When I've something worth two lines.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_good# | #bc_i_hope_so#

scene lake_years
when topic=memories|travel self.away=yes self.from=coldwater
does tell.memory / react.self / assess
a : At home I could see clear across #lake# on a calm day. Here the smoke hides the far end of #walk#. | I left #self.from_town# owing nobody. I mean to go back the same way. | Still water at home. Here everything's on the move, rope and folk alike.
b[from=coldwater] #home : Calm days on the lake. I remember. | Owing nobody. Hard to do. | The still water. I think of it often.
b : Do you miss it? | Will you go back? | Restless, the city.
a@home : Then you'll know the quiet I miss. | Hard, and I'll do it. #oath#. | So do I. More than I'd say to most.
a : Some days. The quiet, mostly. | When #cord#'s bare. Not before. | Restless, and it never pays its debts.

scene talk_slow
when topic=accent self.away=yes self.from=coldwater
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The hands at #walk# say I talk like the lake. Slow, and no waves. | I say calm water to folk at the market. They look at me like I've wished them drowned. | I've kept my lake talk. It's paid for.
b : Do you? | Drowned? | Paid for?
a : I do. I'll not hurry it for them. | They don't know it's a blessing. I don't explain. | Years and years. It's mine, and I owe nobody for it.

scene shut_door
when topic=newcomer|smalltalk
does give.opinion / disagree / insist / ack
a : My door stays shut to faces I've not measured. They're owed nothing, and I'm owed nothing. | On the wharf a stranger wanted a loan off me. I walked on. | New faces every week at #walk#. I learn their names when they've paid a debt.
b : That's cold. | Fair enough. | That's hard on them.
a : It's plain. Plain's not cold. | Fair. I'd not ask it of them either. | It is. #saying.capitalize#. It's fair, though.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_true# | #bc_fair#

scene lean_shift
when topic=times|work world.times=hard|lean self.job=crafter
does tell.worry / reassure / assess / ack
a : Short shifts on #walk#. They're laying off by the day. | Everybody's owing somebody this month. #cord.capitalize#'s heavy. | Hard times. I've had to put a knot on for bread.
b : It'll turn. | Heavy how? | No shame.
a : It will. Ships always want rope. #reassure#. | More knots than I've had in years. | No shame. But I'll pick it out first, before any other.
b? : #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_true#

scene chapel_debt
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : The chapel fed us one winter. I've a knot for it still. | I give at the chapel twice a year. It's #debt# I'll never pay out. | I'm not one for prayer. I'm one for paying what I owe. The Bright One's tally is better kept than mine.
b : That's kind. | Never? | I hope so.
a : It's owed. Kind's got nothing to do with it. | Never. Some knots stay. #oath#. | I'd think so. #bc_true#

story first_debt [topic=memories self.age>=40 self.away=yes]
  : My first debt was a copper off a boatwright in #self.from_town#, when I was small.
  : I tied my first knot for it. It sat on #cord# a long, long while.
  ask : Have you ever owed something that long?
  b : Not that I'd admit.
  b[old] : Longer. Some I'll take with me.
  : I sent it back with a stranger going up the road. Two coppers, for the wait. #saying.capitalize#.

story cable_held [topic=work|memories self.job=crafter self.age>=25]
  : I laid a cable once that held a ship off the rocks in a blow. Or so the skipper said.
  : He came to #walk# after and shook my paw. Wouldn't let go.
  ask : Would you have believed him?
  b : I'd want to.
  : I did. I've no knot for it. Some things are paid in full the first time.

story big_grey_gull [topic=animals|smalltalk self.dislikes=gulls]
  : There's a big grey gull at the works with one bad foot. Took my bread three days running.
  : Fourth day I brought two loaves. One for me, one for it.
  ask : Could you have stayed cross with a thief like that?
  b : Longer than you, I'd think. You fed it?
  b[friends] : Not likely. You fed it, didn't you? Softest thing I've ever heard from you.
  : It's paid for. No more knots. #oath#. It still takes mine, mind.

rule @walk_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=crafter
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Mind the strands! Under tension. | #hemp.capitalize# up. Keep it moving.

rule @gull_bark
when concept=bark self.dislikes=gulls here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Off, you #thief#. | #gulls.capitalize#. I've a stone for you.

rule @knot_bark
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Another knot. #saying.capitalize#. | That's one out. #oath#. Square.

rule @haggle_bark
when concept=bark self.dislikes=haggling here.place=market
does aside
cooldown 10h
say It's the price. Pay it or don't. | #haggle.capitalize# again. Waste of breath.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. What is it? | #greet#. Be quick.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. You owe me nothing, last I checked.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late, #address#. Say it plain.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : I don't know you. What do you want?
dlg @1 resident.job [self.working=yes self.job=crafter] : I lay rope at #self.workplace#. Walk backwards all day. It's honest work.
dlg @2 resident.job : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. That's the job. | #job_busy#
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# | Nothing I'd swear to.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.news] : Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. That's what's said.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'll take it as true once it's paid for.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | Talk weighs nothing and costs plenty. I leave it lie.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. | #farewell#. We're square.
graft resident.hub
choice What's that knotted cord in your paw? -> cord
node cord
say My tally. A knot for every debt. Single, owed to me. Double, I owe. When it's paid, I pick it out. I'll die with it bare, if I can.
mood calm
free
choice Is there a knot for me? -> cord_me
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node cord_me
say Not yet. Keep it that way, and we'll get on.
choice I'll keep it that way. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
